PURPOSE Price one complete package path under Eqs. 37--40 and optionally construct
    supporting vehicle routes without replacing the saved pricing result.
REFERENCES Paper Eqs. 37--40; SubProblemGeneratorPas.cs.
NOTES Each order has a separate pricing solve. Save its path, objective and
    status before the optional support solve; fix all path values in that solve.
INPUT network, target order r, current dual bundle, package branch decisions,
    limits, includeSupport=false; optional node vehicle branches for support.
OUTPUT PackagePricingResult with separate pricingObjective/supportObjective,
    separate statuses, target package path, optional supporting vehicle paths.

PROCEDURE SolveSeparatePackageModel(network,r,duals,packageBranches,limits,
                                    includeSupport=false,vehicleBranches=empty)
    Create binary y[r,i,t,j,t'] for each served-path arc in A_e,r.
    The explicit vo->vd unserved connector is represented by its penalty seed
        route and excluded here. This separates family 13 from the served-path
        model so Eq. 37 retains its stated service term.
    add net outflow over the complete source connector family = 1.
    add net inflow over the complete sink connector family = 1.
    add outgoing flow = incoming flow at every other internal state.
    Include transfer-state/time balance and the complete pickup/delivery path.
    If the storage uses r+ and r- fragments, select them together and match their
        transfer states; do not return an unpaired fragment as a complete q.
    Service-start expression for target r equals 1; for every other order it is 0.
        This is the target-package convention stated after Eq. 37.
    Apply all order-r branch decisions to their full immutable arc record keys:
        forbid -> y=0; force -> y=1 on this required complete order path.
    Preserve epoch commitments and accepted-service obligations.
    Require a single source-to-sink path under the declared time/state ordering;
        for cyclic catalogs, add path/cycle constraints.

    pricingObjective := etaR * SUM_(i,t,j,t') c[r,i,t,j,t']*y[r,i,t,j,t']
                        - u^tau[r].
    FOR every current vehicle route l and supported package arc (i,t,j,t')
        pricingObjective += y[r,i,t,j,t'] *
            (-u^gamma[l,r,i,t,j,t'] + u^alpha[l,r,i,t,j,t']).
    # This is Eq. 37 after substituting its target-package service indicators.
    # The remaining route-indexed dual terms retain the current pool identity.
    Set pricingObjective; optimize within pricing limits.
    Save pricingStatus, pricingSolverBound and incumbent availability immediately.
    IF no incumbent: RETURN no_candidate with pricingStatus and signatures.
    Audit integrality, source/sink, path, transfer times and branch decisions.
    Save all snapped y values and the ordered package path before any second solve.
    savedPricingObjective := evaluate the original pricing expression on this path.
    Require agreement with the first solve's objective within objectiveTolerance.
    physicalPackageCost := SUM original package arc costs, including any penalty.
    result := PackagePricingResult{orderId=r,candidate=packagePath,
        pricingObjective=savedPricingObjective,pricingStatus,pricingSolverBound,
        physicalPackageCost,supportStatus=not_requested,supportObjective=none,
        supportingVehiclePaths=empty,validation=passed,dual/pool/branch signatures}.
    IF includeSupport=false: RETURN result.

    support := BuildSupportingVehiclePaths(network,packagePath,vehicleBranches,limits).
    Copy support.status/objective/paths into the separate support fields.
    Require result.candidate and result.pricingObjective remain unchanged.
    RETURN result even if support fails; report the support failure explicitly.
    # A support solve is an optional route-seeding aid, not Eq. 37 pricing.

PROCEDURE BuildSupportingVehiclePaths(network,fixedPackagePath,vehicleBranches,limits)
    Create a fresh physical vehicle arc model.
    Fix every target package arc to its saved 0/1 value, including the zeros.
    Add one source-to-sink/unused path per physical vehicle, internal balance,
        duty limits, permitted modes, epoch commitments and vehicle arc branches.
    Add the paper's package-to-vehicle support/assignment, capacity and transfer
        conditions for the fixed package path (ArcModel.pseudo, Eq. 13 interface).
    objective := etaK * SUM_k SUM_(i,t,j,t') c[k,i,t,j,t']*vehicleY[k,i,t,j,t'].
    Optimize within support limits and retain a status scoped to this support model.
    IF no feasible incumbent: RETURN support_open_or_infeasible with no paths.
    Independently validate all returned physical paths and their package support.
    RETURN support_feasible, original physical objective and complete vehicle paths.
    # support_seed routes retain the support objective; pricing status comes
    # from the separate reduced-cost solve.

PROCEDURE ExtractPairedPackageRoutes(result)
    Require a validated complete result.candidate for one parent order.
    If represented in two fragments, return the linked r+/r- arc sets together,
        with one parent package coverage coefficient and one selection identity.
    Keep optional supporting vehicle paths under their own physical owners.
    RETURN complete package route plus separately tagged supporting vehicle routes.

STATUS CONTRACT
    Negative valid pricing incumbents may be admitted before optimal termination.
    A nonnegative time-limited incumbent is pricing_open, not exhausted pricing.
    Proven infeasibility exhausts the declared served-path oracle; an allowed
        unserved seed route can still satisfy the master. If a current admissible
        served route contradicts that status, report a model-consistency failure.
    Only the first model's status/bound/objective describe package pricing.
